    "teacher_markdown": "### Teacher Tips\r\n\r\n- **Watch for vague prompts**\r\n  Students may write very general prompts (e.g., “create my webpage”).  \r\n  Encourage them to use their ROPE plan to add **specific layout details and constraints**.  \r\n  If outputs are off, prompt them with: *“What part of your wireframe did the AI not understand?”*\r\n\r\n- **Keep debugging focused**\r\n  Students may try to fix everything at once or repeatedly regenerate full pages.  \r\n  Redirect them to focus on **one mismatch at a time** and make a targeted prompt revision.  \r\n  Ask: *“What is the one change you’re trying to make in this version?”*\r\n\r\n- **Support interpretation of AI output**\r\n  Some students may accept outputs without evaluating them.  \r\n  Push them to compare carefully: *“Where does this match your wireframe? Where does it not?”*  \r\n  If stuck, have them describe their wireframe out loud or ask AI to describe it, then refine from there.\r\n\r\n\r\n- **Support students when AI misinterprets the wireframe**\r\n  If AI isn’t generating what students expect, have them upload their wireframe and prompt AI to describe the layout. Then, have students edit that description and use it to build a clearer prompt. This helps students make their prompts more specific and aligned to their design."
  },
